WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.090
A signed paper.

2
00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.410
A purse of coins.

3
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.960
A gold ring.

4
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:09.970
Lines link them to people: two
friends, a husband and a wife.

5
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.040
Now look at the word bond.

6
00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.240
A legal promise to repay.

7
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.470
Or a tie of love and loyalty.

8
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.700
One friend borrows from the other.

9
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.030
But what exactly does he owe him?

10
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.290
So in this play, is a bond
about money, or about love?

11
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.630
In this mission, you'll step into Venice,

12
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.940
where Antonio lends for free,
and Shylock charges interest.

13
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:36.410
You'll hear a young man ask
his friend to fund his wooing.

14
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.320
And you'll trace three
bonds: a loan, a friendship,

15
00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.790
and a marriage ring.

16
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.110
Your mission: decide whether
a bond is about money,

17
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.300
or about love.
